  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malawi Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Malawi Country Programme works to strengthen the trade competitiveness and regional integration of one of Southern Africa&apos;s most trade-constrained landlocked economies, operating along the Nacala, Beira, and Dar es Salaam corridors since 2020. The Programme targets three interconnected priorities: reducing the time and cost of trade through corridor-based facilitation measures, digital trade solutions, including an electronic data exchange system linking the Malawi Revenue Authority with Tanzania&apos;s customs platform and the development of the Lilongwe Dry Port to improve inland logistics access; strengthening export competitiveness in high-potential value chains, particularly mango and macadamia, through support for internationally recognised testing and certification at the Malawi Bureau of Standards under SADCAS accreditation and the development of over 30 crop-specific export standards; and promoting inclusive trade by supporting small-scale cross-border traders and advancing digital tools such as the MCCCI Single Digital Portal, which allows traders to obtain Certificates of Origin and other trade documents online, reducing compliance costs and administrative burden.</narrative>
  </description>
